---All the customer-modifiable InfluxDB v2 parameters in Timestream for InfluxDB.
---@class aws.timestream_influxdb.InfluxDBv2Parameters
---@field fluxLogEnabled? boolean Include option to show detailed logs for Flux queries.
---@field logLevel? aws.timestream_influxdb.LogLevel|string Log output level. InfluxDB outputs log entries with severity levels greater than or equal to the level specified.
---@field noTasks? boolean Disable the task scheduler. If problematic tasks prevent InfluxDB from starting, use this option to start InfluxDB without scheduling or executing tasks.
---@field queryConcurrency? number Number of queries allowed to execute concurrently. Setting to 0 allows an unlimited number of concurrent queries.
---@field queryQueueSize? number Maximum number of queries allowed in execution queue. When queue limit is reached, new queries are rejected. Setting to 0 allows an unlimited number of queries in the queue.
---@field tracingType? aws.timestream_influxdb.TracingType|string Enable tracing in InfluxDB and specifies the tracing type. Tracing is disabled by default.
---@field metricsDisabled? boolean Disable the HTTP /metrics endpoint which exposes internal InfluxDB metrics.
---@field httpIdleTimeout? aws.timestream_influxdb.Duration Maximum duration the server should keep established connections alive while waiting for new requests. Set to 0 for no timeout.
---@field httpReadHeaderTimeout? aws.timestream_influxdb.Duration Maximum duration the server should try to read HTTP headers for new requests. Set to 0 for no timeout.
---@field httpReadTimeout? aws.timestream_influxdb.Duration Maximum duration the server should try to read the entirety of new requests. Set to 0 for no timeout.
---@field httpWriteTimeout? aws.timestream_influxdb.Duration Maximum duration the server should spend processing and responding to write requests. Set to 0 for no timeout.
---@field influxqlMaxSelectBuckets? number Maximum number of group by time buckets a SELECT statement can create. 0 allows an unlimited number of buckets.
---@field influxqlMaxSelectPoint? number Maximum number of points a SELECT statement can process. 0 allows an unlimited number of points. InfluxDB checks the point count every second (so queries exceeding the maximum aren’t immediately aborted).
---@field influxqlMaxSelectSeries? number Maximum number of series a SELECT statement can return. 0 allows an unlimited number of series.
---@field pprofDisabled? boolean Disable the /debug/pprof HTTP endpoint. This endpoint provides runtime profiling data and can be helpful when debugging.
---@field queryInitialMemoryBytes? number Initial bytes of memory allocated for a query.
---@field queryMaxMemoryBytes? number Maximum total bytes of memory allowed for all running queries. When this limit is reached, new queries are rejected. Setting to 0 allows unlimited memory usage.
---@field queryMemoryBytes? number Maximum bytes of memory allowed for a single query. Must be greater or equal to queryInitialMemoryBytes.
---@field sessionLength? number Specifies the Time to Live (TTL) in minutes for newly created user sessions.
---@field sessionRenewDisabled? boolean Disables automatically extending a user’s session TTL on each request. By default, every request sets the session’s expiration time to five minutes from now. When disabled, sessions expire after the specified session length and the user is redirected to the login page, even if recently active.
---@field storageCacheMaxMemorySize? number Maximum size (in bytes) a shard’s cache can reach before it starts rejecting writes. Must be greater than storageCacheSnapShotMemorySize and lower than instance’s total memory capacity. We recommend setting it to below 15% of the total memory capacity.
---@field storageCacheSnapshotMemorySize? number Size (in bytes) at which the storage engine will snapshot the cache and write it to a TSM file to make more memory available. Must not be greater than storageCacheMaxMemorySize.
---@field storageCacheSnapshotWriteColdDuration? aws.timestream_influxdb.Duration Duration at which the storage engine will snapshot the cache and write it to a new TSM file if the shard hasn’t received writes or deletes.
---@field storageCompactFullWriteColdDuration? aws.timestream_influxdb.Duration Duration at which the storage engine will compact all TSM files in a shard if it hasn't received writes or deletes.
---@field storageCompactThroughputBurst? number Rate limit (in bytes per second) that TSM compactions can write to disk.
---@field storageMaxConcurrentCompactions? number Maximum number of full and level compactions that can run concurrently. A value of 0 results in 50% of runtime.GOMAXPROCS(0) used at runtime. Any number greater than zero limits compactions to that value. This setting does not apply to cache snapshotting.
---@field storageMaxIndexLogFileSize? number Size (in bytes) at which an index write-ahead log (WAL) file will compact into an index file. Lower sizes will cause log files to be compacted more quickly and result in lower heap usage at the expense of write throughput.
---@field storageNoValidateFieldSize? boolean Skip field size validation on incoming write requests.
---@field storageRetentionCheckInterval? aws.timestream_influxdb.Duration Interval of retention policy enforcement checks. Must be greater than 0.
---@field storageSeriesFileMaxConcurrentSnapshotCompactions? number Maximum number of snapshot compactions that can run concurrently across all series partitions in a database.
---@field storageSeriesIdSetCacheSize? number Size of the internal cache used in the TSI index to store previously calculated series results. Cached results are returned quickly rather than needing to be recalculated when a subsequent query with the same tag key/value predicate is executed. Setting this value to 0 will disable the cache and may decrease query performance.
---@field storageWalMaxConcurrentWrites? number Maximum number writes to the WAL directory to attempt at the same time. Setting this value to 0 results in number of processing units available x2.
---@field storageWalMaxWriteDelay? aws.timestream_influxdb.Duration Maximum amount of time a write request to the WAL directory will wait when the maximum number of concurrent active writes to the WAL directory has been met. Set to 0 to disable the timeout.
---@field uiDisabled? boolean Disable the InfluxDB user interface (UI). The UI is enabled by default.

---All the customer-modifiable InfluxDB v3 Core parameters in Timestream for InfluxDB.
---@class aws.timestream_influxdb.InfluxDBv3CoreParameters
---@field queryFileLimit? number Limits the number of Parquet files a query can access. If a query attempts to read more than this limit, InfluxDB 3 returns an error.
---@field queryLogSize? number Defines the size of the query log. Up to this many queries remain in the log before older queries are evicted to make room for new ones.
---@field logFilter? string Sets the filter directive for logs.
---@field logFormat? aws.timestream_influxdb.LogFormats|string Defines the message format for logs.
---@field dataFusionNumThreads? number Sets the maximum number of DataFusion runtime threads to use.
---@field dataFusionRuntimeType? aws.timestream_influxdb.DataFusionRuntimeType|string Specifies the DataFusion tokio runtime type.
---@field dataFusionRuntimeDisableLifoSlot? boolean Disables the LIFO slot of the DataFusion runtime.
---@field dataFusionRuntimeEventInterval? number Sets the number of scheduler ticks after which the scheduler of the DataFusion tokio runtime polls for external events–for example: timers, I/O.
---@field dataFusionRuntimeGlobalQueueInterval? number Sets the number of scheduler ticks after which the scheduler of the DataFusion runtime polls the global task queue.
---@field dataFusionRuntimeMaxBlockingThreads? number Specifies the limit for additional threads spawned by the DataFusion runtime.
---@field dataFusionRuntimeMaxIoEventsPerTick? number Configures the maximum number of events processed per tick by the tokio DataFusion runtime.
---@field dataFusionRuntimeThreadKeepAlive? aws.timestream_influxdb.Duration Sets a custom timeout for a thread in the blocking pool of the tokio DataFusion runtime.
---@field dataFusionRuntimeThreadPriority? number Sets the thread priority for tokio DataFusion runtime workers.
---@field dataFusionMaxParquetFanout? number When multiple parquet files are required in a sorted way (deduplication for example), specifies the maximum fanout.
---@field dataFusionUseCachedParquetLoader? boolean Uses a cached parquet loader when reading parquet files from the object store.
---@field dataFusionConfig? string Provides custom configuration to DataFusion as a comma-separated list of key:value pairs.
---@field maxHttpRequestSize? number Specifies the maximum size of HTTP requests.
---@field forceSnapshotMemThreshold? aws.timestream_influxdb.PercentOrAbsoluteLong Specifies the threshold for the internal memory buffer. Supports either a percentage (portion of available memory) or absolute value in MB–for example: 70% or 100
---@field walSnapshotSize? number Defines the number of WAL files to attempt to remove in a snapshot. This, multiplied by the interval, determines how often snapshots are taken.
---@field walMaxWriteBufferSize? number Specifies the maximum number of write requests that can be buffered before a flush must be executed and succeed.
---@field snapshottedWalFilesToKeep? number Specifies the number of snapshotted WAL files to retain in the object store. Flushing the WAL files does not clear the WAL files immediately; they are deleted when the number of snapshotted WAL files exceeds this number.
---@field preemptiveCacheAge? aws.timestream_influxdb.Duration Specifies the interval to prefetch into the Parquet cache during compaction.
---@field parquetMemCachePrunePercentage? number Specifies the percentage of entries to prune during a prune operation on the in-memory Parquet cache.
---@field parquetMemCachePruneInterval? aws.timestream_influxdb.Duration Sets the interval to check if the in-memory Parquet cache needs to be pruned.
---@field disableParquetMemCache? boolean Disables the in-memory Parquet cache. By default, the cache is enabled.
---@field parquetMemCacheQueryPathDuration? aws.timestream_influxdb.Duration Specifies the time window for caching recent Parquet files in memory.
---@field lastCacheEvictionInterval? aws.timestream_influxdb.Duration Specifies the interval to evict expired entries from the Last-N-Value cache, expressed as a human-readable duration–for example: 20s, 1m, 1h.
---@field distinctCacheEvictionInterval? aws.timestream_influxdb.Duration Specifies the interval to evict expired entries from the distinct value cache, expressed as a human-readable duration–for example: 20s, 1m, 1h.
---@field gen1Duration? aws.timestream_influxdb.Duration Specifies the duration that Parquet files are arranged into. Data timestamps land each row into a file of this duration. Supported durations are 1m, 5m, and 10m. These files are known as “generation 1” files that the compactor in InfluxDB 3 Enterprise can merge into larger generations.
---@field execMemPoolBytes? aws.timestream_influxdb.PercentOrAbsoluteLong Specifies the size of memory pool used during query execution. Can be given as absolute value in bytes or as a percentage of the total available memory–for example: 8000000000 or 10%.
---@field parquetMemCacheSize? aws.timestream_influxdb.PercentOrAbsoluteLong Specifies the size of the in-memory Parquet cache in megabytes or percentage of total available memory.
---@field walReplayFailOnError? boolean Determines whether WAL replay should fail when encountering errors.
---@field walReplayConcurrencyLimit? number Concurrency limit during WAL replay. Setting this number too high can lead to OOM. The default is dynamically determined.
---@field tableIndexCacheMaxEntries? number Specifies the maximum number of entries in the table index cache.
---@field tableIndexCacheConcurrencyLimit? number Limits the concurrency level for table index cache operations.
---@field gen1LookbackDuration? aws.timestream_influxdb.Duration Specifies how far back to look when creating generation 1 Parquet files.
---@field retentionCheckInterval? aws.timestream_influxdb.Duration The interval at which retention policies are checked and enforced. Enter as a human-readable time–for example: 30m or 1h.
---@field deleteGracePeriod? aws.timestream_influxdb.Duration Specifies the grace period before permanently deleting data.
---@field hardDeleteDefaultDuration? aws.timestream_influxdb.Duration Sets the default duration for hard deletion of data.
---@field pluginRepositoryUrl? string Specifies the URL of the repository that InfluxDB downloads plugins from.
---@field pluginRepositorySecretArn? aws.timestream_influxdb.PluginRepositorySecretArn The Amazon Resource Name (ARN) of the Secrets Manager secret that holds your repository access token.

---The compute topology for an InfluxDB 3 Enterprise cluster, expressed as a list of node groups.
---@class aws.timestream_influxdb.InfluxDBv3EnterpriseDeploymentConfiguration
---@field nodeGroups aws.timestream_influxdb.NodeGroupList The node groups that make up the cluster. Across all node groups, the cluster must include 1 to 4 nodes with the INGEST mode, 0 to 14 nodes with the QUERY mode, and exactly one node with the COMPACT mode.

