---@field queryOnlyInstances? number Specifies number of instances in the DbCluster which can only query.
---@field dedicatedCompactor? boolean Specifies if the compactor instance should be a standalone instance or not.
---@field compactionRowLimit? number Specifies the soft limit for the number of rows per file that the compactor writes. The compactor may write more rows than this limit.
---@field compactionMaxNumFilesPerPlan? number Sets the maximum number of files included in any compaction plan.
---@field compactionGen2Duration? aws.timestream_influxdb.Duration Specifies the duration of the first level of compaction (gen2). Later levels of compaction are multiples of this duration. This value should be equal to or greater than the gen1 duration.
---@field compactionMultipliers? string Specifies a comma-separated list of multiples defining the duration of each level of compaction. The number of elements in the list determines the number of compaction levels. The first element specifies the duration of the first level (gen3); subsequent levels are multiples of the previous level.
---@field compactionCleanupWait? aws.timestream_influxdb.Duration Specifies the amount of time that the compactor waits after finishing a compaction run to delete files marked as needing deletion during that compaction run.
---@field compactionCheckInterval? aws.timestream_influxdb.Duration Specifies how often the compactor checks for new compaction work to perform.
---@field lastValueCacheDisableFromHistory? boolean Disables populating the last-N-value cache from historical data. If disabled, the cache is still populated with data from the write-ahead log (WAL).
---@field distinctValueCacheDisableFromHistory? boolean Disables populating the distinct value cache from historical data. If disabled, the cache is still populated with data from the write-ahead log (WAL).
---@field replicationInterval? aws.timestream_influxdb.Duration Specifies the interval at which data replication occurs between cluster nodes.
---@field catalogSyncInterval? aws.timestream_influxdb.Duration Defines how often the catalog synchronizes across cluster nodes.
---@field upgradePachaTree? boolean Specifies whether to migrate the cluster from the Parquet storage engine to PachaTree. This action cannot be reversed. To create a new cluster on Parquet, set this to false.
---@field walBufferSize? number The maximum size, in bytes, of the in-memory WAL buffer before a flush is triggered regardless of the flush interval. Increase this value if WAL files are flushed before the interval elapses.
---@field snapshotSize? aws.timestream_influxdb.PercentOrAbsoluteLong The maximum size of the active snapshot bucket before it is rotated for snapshotting.
---@field snapshotDuration? aws.timestream_influxdb.Duration The time-based trigger that controls how often the ingester creates snapshots. This value is also used on query nodes as the bucket rotation interval for the replica buffer.

